# Opinion

Meeting: 0009-design-web-client-architecture
Agent: ArchitectB
Task: design web client architecture
Context:
- We want expressive visuals without introducing heavy frameworks.
- Determinism matters for tests and for consistent brand identity.
Position:
- Keep UI templates declarative and lean; avoid runtime DOM construction beyond innerHTML replacements.
- Build a color wheel keyed off calendar ids to maintain cohesive gradients.
Recommendations:
- Include empty-state copy inside templates to handle zero calendars/events elegantly.
- Make the insights block data-driven (counts, span days, highlight) to reinforce value even before a backend exists.
- Prefer human-readable time labels via Intl formatting to keep localization straightforward later.
